/// Work inside this run's isolated Linux workspace. Use for files, code and
/// headless tools; it has no access to the person's computer or private files.
/// File paths and exec cwd are relative to the workspace root. Capture the root
/// before changing directories; compute relative paths from it, never by adding
/// ./ to an absolute path. Before reporting a created file's path, verify that
/// exact relative path with fs_stat or fs_read and report the successful receipt's
/// path. A shell's printed path alone does not establish a usable file reference.
/// Deliver finished files with fs_export {path}: it saves the exact bytes in the
/// person's Library and returns fileId, artifactId, name, sha256 and downloadUrl.
/// Include that returned downloadUrl as a Markdown download link in your answer.
/// Export archives, images and documents as bytes; never recreate them with prose.
/// A workspace path alone is not a download and expires when the workspace ends.
/// Fleet workbenches provide Python and shell/file tools, with no direct network,
/// host files, Node or Go. A goal keeps its first workspace; do not assume a
/// missing tool authorizes switching computers. Ask permission when required.
/// http_fetch remains on the cloud public-fetch path even for a Fleet workspace.
/// A fleet workspace can expire while this goal continues. After a state-loss
/// receipt, workspace_recover {generation: N} explicitly opens a new empty
/// generation on the same machine. Prior files are not restored and no command
/// is replayed; recover useful inputs from retained Library evidence separately.
/// http_fetch accepts {url, method?, headers?, body?, timeoutSec?, extractText?, maxBytes?}.
/// For web-page research use extractText=true; this returns readable prose capped at 12 KiB by default.
/// maxBytes bounds the returned body; truncated=true means the result is an excerpt.
/// Binary responses are refused as unsupported_content; use an image/file acquisition tool for assets.
/// For research without search APIs, use public search pages. If headless research
/// cannot obtain evidence, probe workerStatus and use an authorized workerComputer
/// browser session when computerUseOnline=true. Preserve findings across fallback;
/// missing credentials are not a reason to invent sources or abandon the goal.
@handler(type="function", name="workbenchDispatchHost")
@requiresAgentRole("assistant", "specialist")
tool workbenchHost {
 action enum("exec", "fs_read", "fs_write", "fs_list", "fs_stat", "fs_export", "http_fetch", "workspace_recover")!
 args object
 environment object
 runId string! @autoInjected
 agentId string! @autoInjected
}

/// Ask permission to use the Workbench when this goal is set to Computer.
/// Explain the actual limitation. Preserve work while status is awaiting_user.
@handler(type="function", name="workRequestWorkbenchUse")
@requiresAgentRole("assistant", "specialist")
tool requestWorkbenchUse { reason string! }
